description:
Create internal/agent/qa.go with QAAgent that has two modes:
1. WriteTests(ctx, payload) — TDD test generation (from tester.go GenerateTests logic)
2. VerifyTests(ctx, payload) — when coder fails N times, QA checks if tests are correct (from tester.go UpdateTests)
3. Run(ctx, msg) — quality review: code quality, logic, corner cases (from reviewer.go Run logic)

Payloads:
- QATestPayload{ Plan, ProjectContext, StageName string; Files []string }
- QAVerifyTestsPayload{ Failure string; Files, TestFiles []string; ProjectContext string }
- QAReviewPayload{ Files []string; Root, ProjectContext string; Seeds []string }
- QAReviewResult{ Approved bool; MustFix, NiceToHave []string; Unparsed bool; RawOutput string }

The QA agent reuses test execution logic from tester.go (installDeps, run test commands, write test_report.json).
It also reuses review parsing from review_parse.go.
Keep _test.go ownership in QA (coder still blocked from writing test files).

Must use RoleQA from bus types.
